  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe post-install verification in `install.ps1` and `install.sh` only checked the legacy `fcc-*` launchers and asserted `fcc-server --version` == `free-claude-code X`. A fresh install actually creates the full native command family (every `[project.scripts]` entry), but neither installer confirmed the `mcc-*` commands the post-install message tells the user to use.\n\nBoth scripts now verify the native family — `mcc-server`, `mcc-claude`, `mcc-claude-old`, `mcc-codex`, `mcc-pi`, `mcc-init`, `mcc-chatgpt-oauth-login`, `mcc-compact-log`, `mcc-help`, `my-claude-code` — resolve inside the uv tool bin and assert `mcc-server --version` == `my-claude-code <version>`. The legacy `fcc-*` aliases resolve through the same distribution, so they exist as soon as the native family does. Dry-run text updated to match.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Harness fixtures now populate both command families and emit the native version string for `mcc-server`; the `fcc-missing` failure path deletes `mcc-server` and asserts the verify loop stops before the version call.\n- 26 PS1 installer tests pass; the 6 documented pre-existing PowerShell failures are unchanged.\n- `install.ps1` + `install.sh` both parse; `install.sh` behavior verified by Linux CI.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- None beyond the documented pre-existing PowerShell baseline.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
