    "message": "fix(install): verify the mcc-* / my-claude-code command family in both installers\n\nThe post-install verification in install.ps1 and install.sh only checked the\nlegacy fcc-* launchers and asserted `fcc-server --version` ==\n\"free-claude-code X\". A fresh install actually creates the full native\ncommand family (all [project.scripts] entries), but the installer never\nconfirmed the mcc-* commands the post-install message tells the user to use\n— so on Windows a failure to create them would surface as \"fcc-server\" being\npresent while mcc-server is missing, and the version string check was\nchecking the legacy distribution name.\n\nBoth scripts now verify the native family (mcc-server, mcc-claude,\nmcc-claude-old, mcc-codex, mcc-pi, mcc-init, mcc-chatgpt-oauth-login,\nmcc-compact-log, mcc-help, my-claude-code) resolves inside the uv tool bin\nand assert `mcc-server --version` == \"my-claude-code X\". The legacy fcc-*\naliases resolve through the same distribution, so they exist as soon as the\nnative family does; the dry-run text matches.\n\nTest harness fixtures now populate both command families and emit the\nnative version string for mcc-server; the fcc-missing failure path deletes\nmcc-server and asserts the verify loop stops before the version call.\n\nVerified: install.ps1 and install.sh both parse; 26 PS1 installer tests\npass (the 6 documented pre-existing PowerShell failures unchanged); static\ncross-platform assertions still hold. install.sh path is verified by Linux CI.\n\nVersion 5.2.0 -> 5.2.1 (installer verification fix).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
